    "_doc": "The player's own beasts (systems/livestock.js; market and herds panels in ui/actionMenu/livestock.js; drawn on the inner map at their keeping place by ui/innerMapAnimals.js). Bought and sold by the head at a town's livestock market, kept at a place of yours that suits them (places), fed or grazed, bred, aged, shorn and milked by the day. Days: a year is 120 days (world/seasons.js), so ages and lifespans are in game days. space: room one head takes at a place. feed: gold a head a day when it cannot graze (grazing places: the share of feed still bought each season). products: per adult (femaleOnly: hens and milkers) a day, times the season; they go into the herd's store, collected like a property's goods. A livestock property (works) turns its working beasts into its own output instead (the Pasture's wool, the Dairy's cheese, the Ranch's meat, the Horse Ranch's horses): its output scales with the working head kept there against its target (a founding herd of that size comes with the property). slaughter: what butchering one yields (by hand on the inner map, or at the yard from the herds panel). breeding: daily chance for each adult female in its seasons (a male of her kind must be kept with her), young per birth, rest days before the next. market: who sells it (minType, chance by settlement type, likes: terrain where it is common and cheaper; resource: a map resource nearby that always brings it), stock heads by settlement type; price by type, season and how many are left (scarcity). fallback: the inner-map species drawn (and fought) until data/animals.json has one of the same id; scale shrinks it.",
